Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 10:06:31 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 275/348] =?UTF-8?q?Unified:=20the=20parts=20shelf=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20screws,=20nuts,=20washers,=20profiles=20and=20compa?=
 =?UTF-8?q?ny=20parts?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Bundles the Fasteners workbench (shaise/FreeCAD_FastenersWB fddd07af, GPL-2.0-or-later,
runtime files only, unchanged) as Mod/Fasteners. PartsShelf.py (no GUI):
- JIS B 1176/1180/1181/1194/1177/1256/1251 fasteners in M3–M12 with Japanese names
  ("六角穴付きボルト M6×20"); shapes from Fasteners, the spring washer made here
- what a hole is for (tap drill, thread, clearance hole classes 1–3, counterbore,
  countersink → M size), the plates it holds and the thread it goes into, also of other
  parts on the same axis; the standard length; the placement on the axis by SnapMath
- generic aluminium profiles 20/30/40 series, slot 6/8, between two points
- company parts: folders of FCStd/STEP with an optional shelf.csv (UTF-8 or Shift_JIS)
- one hidden original per kind and size, links where used: the BOM counts them

FreeCADCmd -t TestPartsShelf

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
